-- #2110 (row-atom guarantee) fix-round S2-1 — THE CROSS-MODULE CONTROL FOR THE
-- ATOM-GUARANTEE SEED (`deAtomsBefore` / `declEnvRowAtomsChain`).
--
-- 🚨 THIS IS THE DIRECTION A SINGLE-FILE FIXTURE CANNOT SEE.  #2110 shipped with
-- `dataParamRowAtomsRef` and no seed chain, on a comment claiming the table
-- "accumulates across the modules of one run".  It does not: an entry written while
-- checking `w.mdk` is not visible while checking this module, so `paramRowAtomsOf`
-- missed on `Slot` here and `stash` below — the SAME declaration `w.mdk`'s own
-- `mkSlot` accepts verbatim — was REJECTED with the argument-position laundering
-- diagnostic.  Every one of `test/effect_polarity_fixtures/`'s rows is single-file
-- and all twelve stayed green through that gap.
--
-- `Slot`/`Bare` are exported ABSTRACTLY, so their constructors never reach this
-- module's `registerVariants` and the ONLY way `stash` can be accepted is the
-- cross-module seed.  Losing the seed is LOUD here (over-rejection, exit 1, no
-- schemes printed at all), which is what a positive control should be.
--
-- `keep` is the other half of the same claim: `Bare` SWALLOWS its parameter's row,
-- so the seed must publish `Bare`'s (empty) guarantee too rather than publishing
-- "everything is guaranteed".  Its scheme stays row-polymorphic; the REJECT leg for
-- a laundering relay into `Bare` is pinned by `test/typecheck_error_fixtures/` and by
-- this slice's report, because this harness diffs only the entry's SCHEMES and an
-- erroring entry prints none.
import w.{Slot, Bare, mkSlot, mkBare}

stash : (Unit -> <Stdout | e> Unit) -> Slot e
stash f = mkSlot f

keep : (Unit -> <e> Unit) -> Bare e
keep f = mkBare f

shout : Unit -> <Stdout> Unit
shout _ = putStrLn "hi"

pureStash : Slot <>
pureStash = stash shout

main = println 1
